nd regularly  experimented with them throughout his  late teenage years for him this wasn't  just a matter of getting high or trying  to live life more fully it was actually  a coping mechanism that he used to deal  with the pain that his birth parents  abandoned him according to jobs  psychedelics along with Primal screaming  opened up storage trauma in the medulla  and jobs took many of these habits and  beliefs with them to Apple One frowned  upon habit that he took with them was  his tendency to not take showers jobs  believed that his commitment to a vegan  diet meant that he had flushed out all  of the mucus from his body so  theoretically he believed that he  shouldn't have a body odor and that he  didn't need showers in reality this is  not even true vegan diets tend to skew  away from proteins which play a  significant role in the body's  detoxification process so jobs a vegan  diet likely meant that he should have  taken more showers not less and let's  just say his co-workers strongly agreed  another unique trait of jobs was his  tendency to walk around the Barefoot he  felt that walking around helped him  think and be more creative and that  there is some truth to this moving  around it does energize our brains and  it reduces stress making it easier to  focus on singular thoughts and ideas but  jobs didn't just walk around the  Barefoot he did some weird things  Barefoot jobs like to sink his feet into  cold water to de-stress and this seems  completely harmless at first and it  should be if done like a normal person  maybe you could fill a ball up with  water or maybe even buy a pedicure bowl  but instead job sunk his feet into  toilets at the office I suspect that  this only made his body odor worse it  wasn't just his body that he did these  weird experiments on either jobs also  practiced this hippie anti-establishment  mindset and other facets of his life as  well like his car Dobbs wasn't a fan of  having a license plate on his car for  some reason when questioned about it he  simply said that he didn't have a  license plate because he didn't have a  license plate the way that he made this  work was by getting new leases every six  months California law a lot of people  did not have a license plate for the  first six months after getting a new car  and the jobs exploited this loophole  until he died it wasn't till 2019 that  California finally patched this loophole  while all of these likely just seemed  like odd quirks jobs strongly believed  in each and every one of them and these  unorthodox choices carried over to his  medical choices as well  foreign  jobs hippie Behavior itself was extreme  then you haven't heard about his  spiritual life from his college days  jobs was especially interested in  Buddhism this interest was initially  sparked out of necessity as opposed to  curiosity you see it as a broke college  student free food was a gift and one of  the places that offered free food was  the Hare Krishna Temple near Reed  College every Sunday jobs walked seven  miles to the temple just to get free  food but very soon he walked away with  much more than just food jobs became  especially interested in Mahatma Gandhi  and a Hindu Sage named neem Corolla Baba  pretty soon jobs was talking to his  friends about this age and his teachings  and even though most of his friends were  hippies themselves they were pretty open  to the ideas of peace and Enlightenment  eventually they would get to a point  where they wanted to go meet the neem  cruelibaba in real life but they just  had one issue they were still broke but  as fate would have it an opportunity  would Arise at the time jobs was working  as a consultant at a game development  company called Atari one of their most  popular games was pong you've probably  played it pong gave Atari International  notoriety and a company from Germany  would buy a whole Warehouse full of  circuit boards from Atari unfortunately  though Atari didn't quite make a good  first impression given that half the  boards didn't end up working it out of  the box naturally the German company  wasn't very happy and that they wanted  someone to come out there and fix them  initially atari's founder Nolan Bushnell  sent over a tech guide to Germany but  this guy just made things worse so Nolan  turned to jobs he told the jobs that he  would book him a first class round-trip  ticket to Germany and a five-star hotel  if he could go fix this issue jobs  agreed to take the job but he had one  condition he wanted a one-way ticket to  Germany and wanted the rest of the  travel expenses in cash additionally he  negotiated that once the job was done he  was gone and that's exactly what  happened he finished the job in Germany  and went to India with a Dan Kottke  unfortunately though India didn't quite  live up to his Expectations first of all  the guy they were trying to meet name  Crowley Baba had already died a year  before this and that they simply hadn't  heard the news yet jobs also quote found  India far poorer than he imagined and  was struck by the incongruity between  the country's condition and its Heirs of  Holiness but by far the worst part of  the trip was the constant sickness the  duo picked up lice infections and the  worst of Allah uncontrollable diarrhea  by the end of the trip jobs had lost a  bunch of weight but what he didn't lose  was his belief while his belief in  Hinduism decreased his belief in  Buddhism became stronger than ever  thank you  when jobs returned to the United States  He implemented many Buddhist principles  into his day-to-day life one of his  strongest Buddhist beliefs was that  everything happens for a reason and that  nothing is random this was one of the  ways that he coped with being fired from  Apple in the 80s he eventually came to  accept that none of the successes that  followed this event like Pixar and the  iPhone would have taken place if he  hadn't been fired from Apple he also  adopted a much more pragmatic  perspective when it came to death  remembering that I'll be dead soon is  the most important Tola I've ever  encountered to help me make the big  choices in life because almost  everything of all external expectations  all pride of fear of embarrassment or  failure these things just fall away in  the face of death leaving only what is  truly important this was likely one of  the reasons that he refused to get  surgery from his perspective getting  surgery seemed unnatural and intrusive  and that this went against all of his  hippie and the Buddhist beliefs jobs  eventually make the leap though by the  time he died he would go from refusing  treatment to trying to get experimental  treatment in 2009 for example jobs would  travel to Switzerland to experiment with  their radioactive isotope the isotope  was supposed to attack the faulty  hormone producing cells in the body he  would also try to use his money to  accelerate the process of getting a  liver which many people felt was unfair  he didn't cut lines or do anything  illegal but what he did do was sign up  on deliver transplant lists around the  world this increased the chances that he  would get a matching donor somewhere  personally I don't think this is a  problem given that it's only natural  that you try to use all the resources  that you have to try to save your life  but some like to argue that this is not  something that the average person would  be able to do and so it's unethical let  me know which side you guys stand on it  down below but anyway the saddest part  of all of this is that jobs would  eventually regret his early choices he  admitted that he was wrong for rejecting  a professional help and this is just  made it worse by cancer experts  constantly affirming that he could still  be alive if he had just had surgery  earlier but in the end the thing to keep  in mind is that everyone dies at some  point but not everyone lives this  however was never the case with Steve  Jobs since 